Third-party notices
===================

docu.md / markdown-viewer
-------------------------

The rendering engine in `vendor/markdown-viewer/` (a git submodule: this repo's
tree holds only a gitlink pinned by `.gitmodules`, so the upstream history and
its license boundary stay intact) and the static viewer built from it into
`assets/viewer/` come from

    markdown-viewer/markdown-viewer-extension
    https://github.com/markdown-viewer/markdown-viewer-extension

    pinned commit: eca66a1dd07f2cc8d9bac16337d120aae67ff834
    license:       GPL-3.0-only
    upstream LICENSE text: copied verbatim as the `LICENSE` file in this repo.

The engine is vendored unmodified except for two source edits made by
`scripts/patch-vendor.mjs`, which add the `'dsh'` platform to the engine's
platform union:

    vendor/markdown-viewer/src/types/platform.ts       (PlatformType)
    vendor/markdown-viewer/src/utils/platform-info.ts  (PLATFORM_SET)

Everything that adapts the engine to DeepSeek Harness lives outside the vendor
tree, in this repo's own sources:

    viewer/src/webview/api-impl.ts       PlatformAPI implementation (HTTP file/asset access)
    viewer/src/webview/index.ts          platform singleton
    viewer/src/workspace/viewer-embed.ts iframe-side host bridge and renderer wiring
    viewer/build.js                      fork of upstream `vscode/build.js` (offline viewer build)

Because the combined work links GPL-3.0-only code, the whole repository is
distributed under GPL-3.0-only.

Other bundled third-party assets
--------------------------------

`assets/viewer/` additionally contains the upstream build's third-party
resources (themes, locale message catalogs, KaTeX fonts, drawio stencils,
Mermaid). Their licenses come with the upstream package and its dependencies;
the build output ships them unchanged.

DeepSeek Harness client packages (`@deepseek-ai/*`) are used at runtime but are
not redistributed here; they are declared as peer/dev dependencies in
`package.json`.
